  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as both a noun and a suru verb. The derived na-adjective {強制的|きょうせいてき} (compulsory, forced) is also very common. Carries a negative connotation in most contexts, implying that the action goes against the subject's will.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {強制|きょうせい}する: to force, to compel\n- {強制的|きょうせいてき}に: forcibly, compulsorily\n- {強制|きょうせい}{執行|しっこう}: forced execution (legal term)\n- {強制|きょうせい}{送還|そうかん}: forced deportation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {強要|きょうよう}: coercion, demanding (more personal pressure)\n- {義務|ぎむ}: obligation (neutral, institutional)",
